@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+id: 2026-10-16-template-script-sonar-smells
+title: The dev-checkout and test-db scripts from release 2026.10.14 no longer raise SonarCloud smells
+priority: normal
+area: infra
+type: cleanup
+delivery: code-patch
+intent: >
+  The worktree-safe dev Docker scripts added in release 2026.10.14 raised SonarCloud smells as new
+  code in every clone. They are refactored without any change in behaviour or output:
+
+    - scripts/dev-checkout.mjs: lastAssignment() reads each line through a new splitAssignment()
+      helper (key, trimmed value, opening quote, whether that quote stays open), which brings its
+      cognitive complexity under the limit (S3776).
+    - scripts/dev-checkout.sh and scripts/test-db.sh: every function copies its positional
+      parameters into named locals before using them, and test-db.sh reads its command from
+      `COMMAND="${1:-}"` (S7679).
+    - The two `case` statements in dev-checkout.sh without a default branch get an explicit,
+      commented `*) ;;` (S131).
+    - scripts/dev-checkout.spec.mjs checks that test-db.sh's default URL names a test database in
+      a `before()` hook instead of at module top level, so the assertion runs inside the test
+      runner (S8784).
+    - scripts/test-db.sh: the usage comment at the top lists every command the script handles
+      (`start|stop|reset|logs|migrate|url`), and its whitespace-only blank lines are emptied.
+why: >
+  Each clone's SonarCloud analysis reported these as new-code smells in files the template ships,
+  so a project either carried the findings or fixed them locally and drifted from the template,
+  which makes the next template change to these scripts apply less cleanly.
+affectedPaths:
+  - scripts/dev-checkout.mjs
+  - scripts/dev-checkout.sh
+  - scripts/test-db.sh
+  - scripts/dev-checkout.spec.mjs
+verification:
+  - node --test scripts/*.spec.mjs
+  - bash -n scripts/dev-checkout.sh
+  - bash -n scripts/test-db.sh
+  - pnpm exec prettier --check .
+  - pnpm run nestled-doctor
+agentHints:
+  - >
+    A project whose copies of these four files are still 2026.10.14's, unchanged, takes the
+    template's versions verbatim, except for test-db.sh's project-specific lines (the default test
+    port, the default test database name and the test container name), which keep the project's
+    values. Record `applied`.
+  - >
+    A project that already fixed these smells locally converges on the template's versions where
+    they are equivalent (the helper's name and the local variable names may differ), so the next
+    template change to these scripts applies cleanly. Keep any project-specific behaviour. Record
+    `adapted`.
+  - >
+    These are behaviour-preserving refactors: if the project's dev-checkout spec passed before, it
+    must pass after. A failure points at a mis-merged line, not at the note.
